      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine the number of letters Jennie stamped.**\nThe problem states that Jennie puts stamps on one-third of the letters needing stamps.\nTotal letters needing stamps = 60.\nNumber of letters stamped = $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 60$.\nCalculation: $60 \\div 3 = 20$.\nSo, Jennie stamped 20 letters.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the current total number of stamped letters.**\nThe problem states that after stamping, there are 30 letters in the pile of already-stamped letters.\nThis pile consists of the letters she just stamped plus the letters that were already stamped when she began.\nCurrent total stamped = (Letters she just stamped) + (Originally stamped letters).\n$30 = 20 + (\\text{Originally stamped letters})$.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the original number of stamped letters.**\nTo find the number of letters in the pile when Jennie began, subtract the letters she just added from the current total.\nOriginally stamped letters = $30 - 20$.\nCalculation: $30 - 20 = 10$.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThere were 10 letters in the pile of already-stamped letters when Jennie began.\n\n#### 10<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine the number of letters Jennie stamped.**\nThe problem states that Jennie puts stamps on one-third of the letters needing stamps.\nTotal letters needing stamps = 60.\nNumber of letters stamped = $\\frac{1}{3} \\times 60$.\nCalculation: $60 \\div 3 = 20$.\nSo, Jennie stamped 20 letters.\n\n**Step 2: Determine the current total number of stamped letters.**\nThe problem states that after stamping, there are 30 letters in the pile of already-stamped letters.\nThis pile consists of the letters she just stamped plus the letters that were already stamped when she began.\nCurrent total stamped = (Letters she just stamped) + (Originally stamped letters).\n$30 = 20 + (\\text{Originally stamped letters})$.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the original number of stamped letters.**\nTo find the number of letters in the pile when Jennie began, subtract the letters she just added from the current total.\nOriginally stamped letters = $30 - 20$.\nCalculation: $30 - 20 = 10$.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThere were 10 letters in the pile of already-stamped letters when Jennie began.\n\n#### 10",
